{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-20T13:41:46.041Z","author":"codex-sol","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.2-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"ff9efe9e455d247947dc9dbb","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.2-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"high","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Round EZ covers ownership and linked collection leases. In src/mutation.rs, the remaining LockAge::Modified and LockAge::Receipt item writers still write the supplied mutation timestamp into LockPayload.created_at. They share locks with ownership commands, so a strict contender can read an apparently expired timestamp while one of those writes is live. The published pm-cli 2026.11.18 core lock module creates receipts with nowIso() and checks expiry with Date.now(). Add cross-command regression cases that hold a historical writer past the first contender attempt."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-rust-shared-lock-wall-clock"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Use a wall clock for remaining shared item-lock writers"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Separate item-lock receipt timestamps from historical mutation timestamps on the remaining native write paths."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Task"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["follow-up","lock","oracle"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-20T13:41:46.041Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-20T13:41:46.041Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"codex-sol"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Cross-command contention uses current lease timestamps, typed expiry remains intact, and durable history retains the supplied timestamp."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-rust-oracle-1118"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"07cd5c08197664461fe48814a4553525704c5271cab9e12e6b51a0dcfdf2e0a1","item_hash_version":3,"message":"Track cross-command lease behavior discovered in Round EZ","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"unavailable","reason":"harness_unavailable","resolver":"ai_agent_version","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"a63fb459a9d0f8b2c60eaa3e7ec137f60b01a580b3dc1ad1d748ccd3c639095c"}
